{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the bases of the thresholds shook.</b> As though the thresholds moved from their place." "<b>The bases.</b> Known; and some say this word has no cognate." "<b>From the voice.</b> Of the throng that cries." "Now, he said <b>and they shook</b> as a past-tense verb, and behold, 'will be filled with smoke' — for in the holy tongue there is no marker for future tense; and the pattern of the prophets is to intertwine their words."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:30.652011818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}